not a substitute for configuring two active sources with the same priority.
"""
    replacement = anchor + """
Disabled sources reset and migrate with weight 0. When a source is enabled in
the Configurator, its suggested enabled weight is restored; disabling it again
immediately returns the saved weight to 0.

Magnetic field quality is reported separately from freshness and heading
availability. A fresh finite magnetic heading may remain available at displayed
quality 0 with only a one-percent authority floor. This keeps a single-source
heading defined without concealing the warning, and it prevents that source
from outweighing any healthier compass or moving-baseline source. Startup yaw
is seeded only after four fresh fused samples agree within five degrees while
the aircraft is disarmed.
"""
    if anchor not in text:
        raise RuntimeError("HEADING_FUSION priority/weight documentation anchor missing")
    path.write_text(text.replace(anchor, replacement, 1), encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")

    changelog = ROOT / "CHANGELOG.md"
    value = changelog.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    entry = """\n## 4.0.5\n\n- Keep fresh finite magnetic headings available at displayed quality 0 with a
  one-percent authority floor while preserving the field-quality warning.
- Initialize disarmed startup yaw after four stable fresh samples using a
  dedicated state independent of INAV's legacy GPS-heading initialization.
- Reset, migrate and save disabled heading-source weights as 0.
- Retire firmware older than 4.0.5 from the online flasher selection list.
\n"""
    if "## 4.0.5" not in value:
        first_break = value.find("\n", value.find("# "))
        value = value[: first_break + 1] + entry + value[first_break + 1 :]
        changelog.write_text(value, encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")


def write_release_notes() -> None:
    notes = f"""# Flight Commander {VERSION} Beta

This coordinated beta contains Flight Commander Configurator {VERSION} and
MICOAIR743 firmware {VERSION} with the four standard release deliverables.

## Startup heading and stationary fusion

- Retains the accepted onboard IST8310 transform:
  `X = -nativeY`, `Y = -nativeX`, `Z = nativeZ`.
- Retains the 4.0.4 time-based conversion timeout, atomic DRDY/XYZ read and
  nonblocking sensor reset/reconfiguration.
- Separates sample freshness, heading availability, displayed magnetic-field
  quality and fusion authority.
- Keeps a fresh finite magnetic heading available even when the displayed field
  quality is 0%. A one-percent authority floor keeps a single-source fused
  heading defined without hiding the warning or outweighing a healthier source.
- Requires four fresh fused samples that agree within 5 degrees before seeding
  disarmed startup yaw.
- Uses a dedicated Flight Commander startup-initialized state, so INAV's normal
  compass path can no longer set `gpsHeadingInitialized` first and permanently
  block the correct fused-heading seed.
- Startup no longer requires moving the controller before reported yaw catches
  the stationary source heading.

## Heading-source defaults

- Every disabled heading source resets and migrates to weight 0 in firmware.
- MSP configuration writes normalize disabled source weights to 0.
- The Configurator displays and saves disabled weights as 0, and restores the
  suggested enabled weight when the source is turned on.

